{
  "uid": "platform-golden-signals",
  "title": "Platform — golden signals",
  "description": "RED per service, plus the two §13.7 rows that read request.duration. Owned by Platform (§13.8). Checked into deploy/observability because a dashboard clicked together in a UI is lost with the instance and cannot be reviewed.",
  "tags": ["platform", "red", "slo"],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": { "from": "now-6h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "service",
        "label": "Service",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
        "query": "label_values(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count, service_name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true
      },
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Rate, errors, duration",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request rate",
      "description": "Requests per second per service. Read this first when investigating a business-volume alert: a service nobody can reach has an excellent error rate.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Error ratio (5xx)",
      "description": "The ErrorRate alert fires above the 1% line. 4xx is deliberately excluded — §10.5 maps Error.Rule to 422 and ValidationException to 400, both of which are the system correctly refusing a request.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 8, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.01 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", http_response_status_code=~\"5..\"}[5m])) / sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency p99",
      "description": "The Latency alert fires above 1s. §13.7's targets sit an order of magnitude below this line, so a p99 near it is already far out.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 8, "x": 16, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 1 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (service_name, le) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\"}[10m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Refusals — the failures no error graph shows",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 9 }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "422 — refused by the domain",
      "description": "§6.6's worked case: ordering.ProductPrices has no row for a product, every order containing it is refused, and the customer sees a 422 with no exception, no 5xx and no lag. Not a 400 — the request is well-formed and the validator passed it, so a 400 panel shows a path this request never took.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 10 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service_name, http_route) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", http_response_status_code=\"422\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}} {{http_route}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "401 — rejected before the domain",
      "description": "Every service re-validates independently (§11.4), so an identity-provider fault shows up everywhere at once. A platform full of 401s and no orders is the auth branch of docs/runbooks/business-volume.md.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 10 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps" }, "overrides": [] },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (service_name) (rate(http_server_request_duration_seconds_count{service_name=~\"$service\", http_response_status_code=\"401\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "§13.7 — the two request rows",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 18 }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Command p95 (target 100 ms)",
      "description": "request.duration, filtered to command types. RequestMetrics tags `request` with the type name and carries no kind tag, so the split is by §6.2's naming convention — a request type named otherwise is invisible here.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 19 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.1 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service_name, le) (rate(request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\", request=~\".+Command\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Query p95 (target 80 ms)",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 19 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "red", "value": 0.08 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (service_name, le) (rate(request_duration_seconds_bucket{service_name=~\"$service\", request=~\".+Query\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service_name}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
